-> Reference: particle types — built from the predefined `Particle` base
-> (`_class`/`_created`) merged with field constraints via `∩`, `_class`
-> pinned explicitly. Construction validates fields; `...` spreads an
-> existing particle's fields; `∪ Null` marks a field optional.
Point = Particle ∩ { _class ∈ "Point", x ∈ Number, y ∈ Number }
p = Point { x = 1, y = 2 }
assert p._class = "Point"
assert p.x = 1

q = Point { ...p, y = 9 }
assert q.x = 1
assert q.y = 9

Labeled = Particle ∩ { _class ∈ "Labeled", x ∈ Number, y ∈ Number, label ∈ String ∪ Null }
r = Labeled { x = 0, y = 0 }
assert r.label = Null
